@startuml parking
title Parking protocol — the four steps of design/execution.md

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

legend left
  |= colour |= whose code the box is (dev/ARCHITECTURE.md) |
  |<#DDEBF7>  | unit — the record mechanics and the suspension |
  |<#E2EFDA>  | the armer of the entry — sync, reactor, the actor call |
  |<#FCE4D6>  | sched — the enqueue |
  Every step runs on the unit's own thread; the split is by whose code
  runs, not by which thread. Step 3 is the unit's own suspension, step 4
  is the worker's, and the stores of step 4 are unit record operations
  the worker calls. Retirement is a unit operation too, and the handle
  body it invokes belongs to the armer.
endlegend

start

#DDEBF7:**1. Write the record**
a fresh epoch, the entries, the mode,
and remaining for an AND wait.
The only place the epoch is written:
no path that ends a wait touches it;

note right
  Arming after the record is written is what
  guarantees a completion finds somewhere
  to record itself.
end note

partition "**2. Arm each entry**, one at a time" {
  while (entries left to arm?) is (yes)
    #E2EFDA:submit the operation, send the message
    or arm the timer — carrying the unit, its
    entry index and the epoch of step 1;
    #E2EFDA:install this entry's cancel handle;
    if (satisfied inline?) then (yes)
      if (OR, or AND with nothing left outstanding?) then (the wait is over)
        #DDEBF7:retire every entry armed so far,
        this one included.
        The entries after it were never armed;
        #DDEBF7:continue without suspending —
        step 3 is skipped;
        stop
      else (AND, entries still outstanding)
        #DDEBF7:retire nothing and go on arming;
      endif
    else (no)
    endif
  endwhile (no)
}

#DDEBF7:**3. Suspend**
stackful: switch to the worker.
stackless: return Pending from poll;

note right
  Step 4 is the worker's, not the unit's: a unit
  that announced itself parked while its machine
  context was still being saved would be resumable
  before it was savable.
end note

if (is the cancelled bit set?) then (no)
  #DDEBF7:**4. Store Parked**;
  stop
else (yes)
  #DDEBF7:store the cancellation in the
  record's own result slot;
  #DDEBF7:claim the winner with the
  reserved no-entry value;
  note right
    The claim comes before the retirement.
    Retirement is asynchronous, and an entry
    armed at step 2 that fires afterwards is
    rejected by the claim and by nothing else —
    the epoch is the one just written.
  end note
  #DDEBF7:retire the entries
  through their cancel handles;
  #DDEBF7:store Woken —
  this unit is never Parked;
  #FCE4D6:enqueue into this worker's list;
  stop
endif

@enduml
